# MQTT topic ACL — the broker is a control-plane boundary (SDLC 08).
# Least privilege: each identity may touch only the topics its role needs.
# Prod equivalent: AWS IoT Core policies (10-aws-deployment §4).

# backend — consumes the whole site namespace, is the ONLY writer of commands.
user backend
topic read plant1/#
topic write plant1/cmd/#

# edge1 — reads its own command queue, writes its own responses,
# heartbeat, and telemetry. Cannot publish commands or read cmd-resp.
user edge1
topic read plant1/cmd/edge1/#
topic write plant1/cmd-resp/edge1/#
topic write plant1/edge/edge1/#
topic write plant1/sort/#

# tester — integration-test fault-injection identity. Tests impersonate
# every actor: publish commands (backend role), publish telemetry and
# malformed payloads (edge role), and subscribe to responses. Wide by
# design — this identity must never exist outside the demo passwd file.
user tester
topic read $SYS/broker/uptime
topic readwrite plant1/#
